\s1 David Arranges Uriah’s Death
\p \v 14 \w -|strong="H01961"\w* \w The next morning|strong="H01242"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w wrote|strong="H03789"\w* \w a letter|strong="H05612"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w and sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03027"\w* \w it with Uriah|strong="H00223"\w*. \v 15 \w In the letter|strong="H05612"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w* \w he wrote|strong="H03789"\w*: “\w Put|strong="H03051"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w at|strong="H00413"\w* \w the front|strong="H04136"\w* \w . . .|strong="H06440"\w* \w of the fiercest|strong="H02389"\w* \w battle|strong="H04421"\w*; \w then withdraw|strong="H07725"\w* \w from him|strong="H00310"\w*, \w so that he may be struck down|strong="H05221"\w* \w and killed|strong="H04191"\w*.”
\p \v 16 \w So as|strong="H01961"\w* \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w besieged|strong="H08104"\w* \w -|strong="H00413"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w*, \w he assigned|strong="H05414"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w a place|strong="H04725"\w* \w where|strong="H00834"\w* \w he knew|strong="H03045"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03588"\w* \w the strongest enemy soldiers [were]|strong="H00582"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02428"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08033"\w*. \v 17 \w And when the men|strong="H00582"\w* \w of the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w came out|strong="H03318"\w* \w and fought|strong="H03898"\w* \w against|strong="H00854"\w* \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w*, \w some of|strong="H04480"\w* \w David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w vvv|strong="H05971"\w* \w servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w fell|strong="H05307"\w*, \w and Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H02850"\w* \w also|strong="H01571"\w* \w died|strong="H04191"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05046"\w* \w to David|strong="H01732"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w a full account|strong="H03605"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01697"\w* \w of the battle|strong="H04421"\w* \v 19 \w and instructed|strong="H06680"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the messenger|strong="H04397"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w* “\w When you have finished|strong="H03615"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w giving|strong="H01696"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w a full|strong="H03605"\w* \w account|strong="H01697"\w* \w of the battle|strong="H04421"\w*, \v 20 \w -|strong="H01961"\w* \w if|strong="H00518"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w anger|strong="H02534"\w* \w flares|strong="H05927"\w*, \w he may ask|strong="H00559"\w* you, ‘\w Why|strong="H04069"\w* \w did you get so close|strong="H05066"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w to fight|strong="H03898"\w*? \w Did you not|strong="H03808"\w* \w realize|strong="H03045"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w they would shoot|strong="H03384"\w* \w from atop|strong="H05921"\w* \w the wall|strong="H02346"\w*? \v 21 \w Who|strong="H04310"\w* \w struck|strong="H05221"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Abimelech|strong="H00040"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Jerubbesheth|strong="H03380"\w*\f + \fr 11:21 \fqa Jerubbesheth \ft is also known as \fqa Jerubbaal\ft , that is, Gideon.\f*? \w Was it not|strong="H03808"\w* \w a woman|strong="H00802"\w* \w who dropped|strong="H07993"\w* \w an upper millstone|strong="H06400"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07393"\w* \w on him|strong="H05921"\w* \w from|strong="H05921"\w* \w the wall|strong="H02346"\w*, \w so that he died|strong="H04191"\w* \w in Thebez|strong="H08405"\w*? \w Why|strong="H04100"\w* \w did you get so close|strong="H05066"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the wall|strong="H02346"\w*?’
\p \w [If he asks you this,] then you are to say|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w Your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H02850"\w* \w is dead|strong="H04191"\w* \w as well|strong="H01571"\w*.’”
\p \v 22 \w So the messenger|strong="H04397"\w* \w set out|strong="H01980"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00935"\w* \w and reported|strong="H05046"\w* \w to David|strong="H01732"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w had sent him to say|strong="H07971"\w*. \v 23 \w The messenger|strong="H04397"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H03588"\w* “\w The men|strong="H00582"\w* \w overpowered us|strong="H01396"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w and came out|strong="H03318"\w* \w against us|strong="H00413"\w* \w in the field|strong="H07704"\w*, \w but we drove them back|strong="H01961"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w to|strong="H05704"\w* \w the entrance|strong="H06607"\w* \w of the gate|strong="H08179"\w*. \v 24 \w Then the archers|strong="H03384"\w* \w shot|strong="H03384"\w* \w at|strong="H00413"\w* \w your servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w from|strong="H05921"\w* \w the wall|strong="H02346"\w*, \w and some of the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w were killed|strong="H04191"\w*. \w And your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H02850"\w* \w is dead|strong="H04191"\w* \w as well|strong="H01571"\w*.”
\p \v 25 \w Then David|strong="H01732"\w* \w told|strong="H00559"\w* \w -|strong="H00413"\w* \w the messenger|strong="H04397"\w*, “\w Say|strong="H00559"\w* \w this|strong="H03541"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w*: ‘\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w let this|strong="H02088"\w* \w matter|strong="H01697"\w* \w upset|strong="H07489"\w* \w you|strong="H05869"\w*, \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w the sword|strong="H02719"\w* \w devours|strong="H00398"\w* \w one|strong="H02088"\w* \w as well as another|strong="H02090"\w*. \w Strengthen|strong="H02388"\w* \w your attack|strong="H04421"\w* \w against|strong="H00413"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w and demolish it|strong="H02040"\w*.’ \w Encourage him [with these words]|strong="H02388"\w*.”
\s1 David Marries Bathsheba
\p \v 26 \w When Uriah’s|strong="H00223"\w* \w wife|strong="H00802"\w* \w heard|strong="H08085"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w her husband|strong="H00376"\w* \w -|strong="H00223"\w* \w was dead|strong="H04191"\w*, \w she mourned|strong="H05594"\w* \w for|strong="H05921"\w* \w him|strong="H01167"\w*. \v 27 \w And when the [time of] mourning|strong="H00060"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07971"\w* \w was over|strong="H05674"\w*, \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w had her brought|strong="H00622"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w his house|strong="H01004"\w*, \w and she became|strong="H01961"\w* his \w wife|strong="H00802"\w* \w and bore|strong="H03205"\w* him \w a son|strong="H01121"\w*.
\p \w But the thing|strong="H01697"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w had done|strong="H06213"\w* \w was evil|strong="H07489"\w* \w in the sight|strong="H05869"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*.
\c 12
\s1 Nathan Rebukes David
\r (Psalm 51:1–19)
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w Nathan|strong="H05416"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w*, \w and when he arrived|strong="H00935"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w*, \w he said|strong="H00559"\w* -, “\w There were|strong="H01961"\w* \w two|strong="H08147"\w* \w men|strong="H00582"\w* \w in a certain|strong="H00259"\w* \w city|strong="H05892"\w*, \w one|strong="H00259"\w* \w rich|strong="H06223"\w* \w and the other|strong="H00259"\w* \w poor|strong="H07326"\w*. \v 2 \w The rich|strong="H06223"\w* \w man had|strong="H01961"\w* \w a great number of|strong="H07235"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03966"\w* \w sheep|strong="H06629"\w* \w and cattle|strong="H01241"\w*, \v 3 \w but the poor|strong="H07326"\w* \w man had nothing|strong="H00369"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03605"\w* \w except|strong="H03588"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00518"\w* \w one|strong="H00259"\w* \w small|strong="H06996"\w* \w ewe lamb|strong="H03535"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w he had bought|strong="H07069"\w*. \w He raised it|strong="H02421"\w*, \w and it grew up|strong="H01431"\w* \w with him|strong="H05973"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05973"\w* \w and his children|strong="H01121"\w*. \w It shared|strong="H03162"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00398"\w* \w his food|strong="H06595"\w* \w and drank|strong="H08354"\w* \w from his cup|strong="H03563"\w*; \w it slept|strong="H07901"\w* \w in his arms|strong="H02436"\w*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa in his bosom\ft ; also in verse 8\f* \w and was|strong="H01961"\w* \w like a daughter|strong="H01323"\w* to him.
\p \v 4 \w Now a traveler|strong="H01982"\w* \w came|strong="H00935"\w* \w to the rich|strong="H06223"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02550"\w* \w man|strong="H00376"\w*, \w who refrained from taking|strong="H03947"\w* \w one of his own sheep|strong="H06629"\w* \w or cattle|strong="H01241"\w* \w to prepare|strong="H06213"\w* \w for the traveler|strong="H00732"\w* \w who had come|strong="H00935"\w* to him. \w Instead, he took|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the poor|strong="H07326"\w* \w man’s|strong="H00376"\w* \w lamb|strong="H03535"\w* \w and prepared it|strong="H06213"\w* \w for his guest|strong="H00376"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00935"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w*.”
\p \v 5 \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w burned|strong="H02734"\w* \w with anger|strong="H00639"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03966"\w* \w against the man|strong="H00376"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Nathan|strong="H05416"\w*: “\w As surely as the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03588"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01121"\w* \w lives|strong="H02416"\w*, \w the man|strong="H00376"\w* \w who did|strong="H06213"\w* \w this|strong="H02063"\w* \w deserves to die|strong="H04194"\w*! \v 6 \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Because|strong="H06118"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w he has done|strong="H06213"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w this|strong="H02088"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w thing|strong="H01697"\w* \w and has shown no|strong="H03808"\w* \w pity|strong="H02550"\w*, \w he must pay|strong="H07999"\w* \w for the lamb|strong="H03535"\w* \w four times over|strong="H00706"\w*.”
\p \v 7 \w Then Nathan|strong="H05416"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w*, “\w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w are that man|strong="H00376"\w*! \w This is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w says|strong="H00559"\w*: ‘\w I|strong="H00595"\w* \w anointed|strong="H04886"\w* \w you king|strong="H04428"\w* \w over|strong="H05921"\w* \w Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w and I|strong="H00595"\w* \w delivered you|strong="H05337"\w* \w from the hand|strong="H03027"\w* \w of Saul|strong="H07586"\w*. \v 8 \w I gave|strong="H05414"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w your master’s|strong="H00113"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w house to you|strong="H01004"\w* \w and your master’s|strong="H00113"\w* \w wives|strong="H00802"\w* \w into your arms|strong="H02436"\w*. \w I gave|strong="H05414"\w* you \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w and Judah|strong="H03063"\w*, \w and if|strong="H00518"\w* \w that was not enough|strong="H04592"\w*, \w I would have given|strong="H03254"\w* you even more . . ..
\p \v 9 \w Why|strong="H04069"\w* \w then have you despised|strong="H00959"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the command|strong="H01697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w by doing|strong="H06213"\w* \w evil|strong="H07451"\w* \w in His sight|strong="H05869"\w*? \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w You put|strong="H05221"\w* \w Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H02850"\w* \w to the sword|strong="H02719"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and took|strong="H03947"\w* \w his wife|strong="H00802"\w* \w as your own|strong="H00802"\w*. \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w You have slain him|strong="H02026"\w* \w with the sword|strong="H02719"\w* \w of the Ammonites|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05983"\w*. \v 10 \w Now, therefore|strong="H06258"\w*, \w the sword|strong="H02719"\w* \w will never|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05704"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05769"\w* \w depart|strong="H05493"\w* \w from your house|strong="H01004"\w*, \w because|strong="H06118"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03588"\w* \w you have despised Me|strong="H00959"\w* \w and have taken|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the wife|strong="H00802"\w* \w of Uriah|strong="H00223"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H02850"\w* \w to be|strong="H01961"\w* your \w own|strong="H00802"\w*.’
\p \v 11 \w This is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02005"\w* \w says|strong="H00559"\w*: ‘\w I will raise up|strong="H06965"\w* \w adversity|strong="H07451"\w* \w against you|strong="H05921"\w* \w from your own house|strong="H01004"\w*. \w Before your very eyes|strong="H05869"\w* \w I will take|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w your wives|strong="H00802"\w* \w and give them|strong="H05414"\w* \w to another|strong="H07453"\w*, \w and he will lie|strong="H07901"\w* \w with them|strong="H05973"\w* \w in broad daylight|strong="H00802"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05869"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02063"\w*. \v 12 \w -|strong="H03588"\w* \w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w have acted|strong="H06213"\w* \w in secret|strong="H05643"\w*, \w but I|strong="H00589"\w* \w will do|strong="H06213"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H01697"\w* \w this thing|strong="H02088"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05048"\w* \w in broad daylight|strong="H08121"\w* \w before|strong="H05048"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H03478"\w*.’”
\s1 David’s Loss and Repentance
\p \v 13 \w Then David|strong="H01732"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Nathan|strong="H05416"\w*, “\w I have sinned|strong="H02398"\w* \w against the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*.”
\p “\w The LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w has taken away|strong="H05674"\w* \w your sin|strong="H02403"\w*,” \w Nathan|strong="H05416"\w* \w replied|strong="H00559"\w* \w -|strong="H00413"\w* \w -|strong="H01732"\w*. \w -|strong="H01571"\w* “\w You will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w die|strong="H04191"\w*. \v 14 \w Nevertheless|strong="H00657"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w by|strong="H02088"\w* \w -|strong="H01571"\w* \w this deed|strong="H01697"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05006"\w* \w you have shown utter contempt|strong="H05006"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w for [the word]|strong="H00341"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*,\f + \fr 12:14 \ft DSS; MT \fqa you have brought utter contempt from the enemies of the LORD\f* \w the son|strong="H01121"\w* \w born|strong="H03209"\w* to you \w will surely die|strong="H04191"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04191"\w*.”
\p \v 15 \w After Nathan|strong="H05416"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w had gone|strong="H01980"\w* \w home|strong="H01004"\w*, \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w struck|strong="H05062"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w Uriah’s|strong="H00223"\w* \w wife|strong="H00802"\w* \w had borne|strong="H03205"\w* \w to David|strong="H01732"\w*, \w and he became ill|strong="H00605"\w*. \v 16 \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w pleaded|strong="H01245"\w* \w with God|strong="H00430"\w* \w for|strong="H01157"\w* \w the boy|strong="H05288"\w*. \w He|strong="H01732"\w* \w fasted|strong="H06684"\w* \w . . .|strong="H06685"\w* \w and went into his house|strong="H00935"\w* \w and spent the night|strong="H03885"\w* \w lying [in sackcloth]|strong="H07901"\w*\f + \fr 12:16 \ft DSS and LXX; MT does not include \fqa in sackcloth\ft .\f* \w on the ground|strong="H00776"\w*. \v 17 \w The elders|strong="H02205"\w* \w of his household|strong="H01004"\w* \w stood|strong="H06965"\w* \w beside him|strong="H05921"\w* \w to help him up|strong="H06965"\w* \w from|strong="H04480"\w* \w the ground|strong="H00776"\w*, \w but he was unwilling|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00014"\w* \w and would not|strong="H03808"\w* \w eat|strong="H01254"\w* \w anything with them|strong="H00854"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03899"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w . . .|strong="H01961"\w* \w On the seventh|strong="H07637"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w died|strong="H04191"\w*. \w But David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w were afraid|strong="H03372"\w* \w to tell|strong="H05046"\w* him \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w was dead|strong="H04191"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w they said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Look|strong="H02009"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H01961"\w* \w while the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w was alive|strong="H02416"\w*, \w we spoke|strong="H01696"\w* \w to him|strong="H00413"\w*, \w and he would not|strong="H03808"\w* \w listen to us|strong="H08085"\w*. \w . . .|strong="H06963"\w* \w So how|strong="H00349"\w* \w can we tell|strong="H00559"\w* \w him|strong="H00413"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w is dead|strong="H04191"\w*? \w He may even harm himself|strong="H06213"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07451"\w*.”
\p \v 19 \w When David|strong="H01732"\w* \w saw|strong="H07200"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w his servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w were whispering to one another|strong="H03907"\w*, \w he|strong="H01732"\w* \w perceived|strong="H00995"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w was dead|strong="H04191"\w*. \w So he|strong="H01732"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w asked|strong="H00559"\w* \w his servants|strong="H05650"\w*, “\w Is the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w dead|strong="H04191"\w*?”
\p “\w He is dead|strong="H04191"\w*,” \w they replied|strong="H00559"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w Then David|strong="H01732"\w* \w got up|strong="H06965"\w* \w from the ground|strong="H00776"\w*, \w washed|strong="H07364"\w* \w and anointed himself|strong="H05480"\w*, \w changed|strong="H02498"\w* \w his clothes|strong="H08071"\w*, \w and went into|strong="H00935"\w* \w the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w and worshiped|strong="H07812"\w*. \w Then he went|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w his own house|strong="H01004"\w*, \w and at his request|strong="H07592"\w* \w they set|strong="H07760"\w* \w food|strong="H03899"\w* before him, \w and he ate|strong="H00398"\w*.
\p \v 21 “\w What [is]|strong="H04100"\w*\w . . .|strong="H01697"\w* \w this|strong="H02088"\w*\w . . .|strong="H00834"\w* \w you have done|strong="H06213"\w*?” \w his servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w asked|strong="H00559"\w*. “\w While|strong="H05668"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w was alive|strong="H02416"\w*, \w you fasted|strong="H06684"\w* \w and wept|strong="H01058"\w*, \w but when|strong="H00834"\w* \w he|strong="H03206"\w* \w died|strong="H04191"\w*, \w you got up|strong="H06965"\w* \w and ate|strong="H00398"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03899"\w*.”
\p \v 22 \w [David] answered|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w While|strong="H05750"\w* \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w was alive|strong="H02416"\w*, \w I fasted|strong="H06684"\w* \w and wept|strong="H01058"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w I said|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w Who|strong="H04310"\w* \w knows|strong="H03045"\w*? \w The LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w may be gracious|strong="H02603"\w* \w to me|strong="H03206"\w* \w and let him live|strong="H02421"\w*.’ \v 23 \w But now|strong="H06258"\w* \w that he is dead|strong="H04191"\w*, \w why|strong="H04100"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02088"\w* \w should I|strong="H00589"\w* \w fast|strong="H06684"\w*? \w Can|strong="H03201"\w* \w I bring him back|strong="H07725"\w* \w again|strong="H05750"\w*? \w I will|strong="H00589"\w* \w go|strong="H01980"\w* \w to him|strong="H00413"\w*, \w but he|strong="H01931"\w* \w will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w return|strong="H07725"\w* \w to me|strong="H00413"\w*.”
\s1 Solomon’s Birth
\p \v 24 \w Then David|strong="H01732"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01339"\w* \w comforted|strong="H05162"\w* \w his wife|strong="H00802"\w* \w Bathsheba|strong="H01339"\w*, \w and he went|strong="H00935"\w* \w to her|strong="H00413"\w* \w and lay|strong="H07901"\w* \w with her|strong="H05973"\w*. \w So she gave birth to|strong="H03205"\w* \w a son|strong="H01121"\w*, \w and they|strong="H07121"\w*\f + \fr 12:24 \ft Or \fqa she \ft or \fqa he\f* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w named him|strong="H08034"\w* \w Solomon|strong="H08010"\w*.
\p \w Now the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w loved [the child]|strong="H00157"\w* \v 25 \w and sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w [word] through|strong="H03027"\w* \w Nathan|strong="H05416"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H05030"\w* \w to name him|strong="H07121"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H08034"\w* \w Jedidiah|strong="H03041"\w* \w because|strong="H05668"\w* \w the LORD [loved him]|strong="H03068"\w*.\f + \fr 12:25 \ft Literally \fqa to name him Jedidiah because of the LORD\ft ; \fqa Jedidiah \ft means \fqa beloved of the LORD\f*
\s1 The Capture of Rabbah
\r (1 Chronicles 20:1–3)
\p \v 26 \w Meanwhile, Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w fought|strong="H03898"\w* \w against Rabbah|strong="H07237"\w* \w of the Ammonites|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05983"\w* \w and captured|strong="H03920"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the royal|strong="H04410"\w* \w fortress|strong="H05892"\w*. \v 27 \w Then Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w messengers|strong="H04397"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w to say|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w I have fought|strong="H03898"\w* \w against Rabbah|strong="H07237"\w* \w and have|strong="H01571"\w* \w captured|strong="H03920"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the water [supply]|strong="H04325"\w* \w of the city|strong="H05892"\w*.\f + \fr 12:27 \ft Or \fqa and have captured the city of waters\f* \v 28 \w Now, therefore|strong="H06258"\w*, \w assemble|strong="H00622"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the rest|strong="H03499"\w* \w of the troops|strong="H05971"\w*, \w lay siege|strong="H02583"\w* \w to|strong="H05921"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w*, \w and capture it|strong="H03920"\w*. \w Otherwise|strong="H06435"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w will capture|strong="H03920"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w*, \w and it will be named|strong="H07121"\w* \w after me|strong="H08034"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w*.”
\p \v 29 \w So David|strong="H01732"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w assembled|strong="H00622"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the troops|strong="H05971"\w* \w and went|strong="H01980"\w* \w to Rabbah|strong="H07237"\w*; \w and he fought|strong="H03898"\w* against it \w and captured it|strong="H03920"\w*. \v 30 \w Then he took|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the crown|strong="H05850"\w* \w from|strong="H05921"\w* \w the head|strong="H07218"\w* \w of their king|strong="H04428"\w*.\f + \fr 12:30 \ft Or \fqa from the head of Milcom\ft . Milcom, also called Molech, was god of the Ammonites; see Leviticus 18:21 and 1 Kings 11:7.\f* \w It weighed|strong="H04948"\w* \w a talent|strong="H03603"\w* \w of gold|strong="H02091"\w*\f + \fr 12:30 \fqa A talent \ft is approximately 75.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f* \w and was set with precious|strong="H03368"\w* \w stones|strong="H00068"\w*, \w and it was|strong="H01961"\w* \w placed on|strong="H05921"\w* \w David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w head|strong="H07218"\w*. \w And David took|strong="H03318"\w* \w a great amount|strong="H07235"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03966"\w* \w of plunder|strong="H07998"\w* \w from the city|strong="H05892"\w*.
\p \v 31 \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w [David] brought out|strong="H03318"\w* \w the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w who [were]|strong="H00834"\w* there \w and put [them to work]|strong="H07760"\w* \w with saws|strong="H04050"\w*,\f + \fr 12:31 \ft Literally \fqa put them under saws\f* \w iron|strong="H01270"\w* \w picks|strong="H02757"\w*, \w and axes|strong="H04037"\w* \w -|strong="H01270"\w*, \w and he made them work|strong="H05674"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w at the brick kilns|strong="H04404"\w*.\f + \fr 12:31 \ft Literally \fqa and he made them pass through the brick kilns.\f* \w He did|strong="H06213"\w* \w the same|strong="H03651"\w* \w to all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the Ammonite|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05983"\w* \w cities|strong="H05892"\w*. \w Then [David]|strong="H01732"\w* \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w his troops|strong="H05971"\w* \w returned|strong="H07725"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w*.
\c 13
\s1 Amnon and Tamar
\p \v 1 \w After some time|strong="H01961"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00310"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03651"\w*, \w David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w fell in love|strong="H00157"\w* \w with Tamar|strong="H08559"\w*, \w the beautiful|strong="H03303"\w* \w sister|strong="H00269"\w* \w -|strong="H08034"\w* \w of David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w Absalom|strong="H00053"\w*. \v 2 \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w was sick|strong="H02470"\w* \w with frustration|strong="H03334"\w* \w over|strong="H05668"\w* \w his sister|strong="H00269"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w she|strong="H01931"\w* \w was a virgin|strong="H01330"\w*, \w and it seemed|strong="H05869"\w* \w implausible|strong="H06381"\w* \w for [him]|strong="H00550"\w* \w to do|strong="H06213"\w* \w anything|strong="H03972"\w* to her.
\p \v 3 \w Now Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w had a friend|strong="H07453"\w* \w named|strong="H08034"\w* \w Jonadab|strong="H03122"\w*, \w the son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Shimeah|strong="H08093"\w*.\f + \fr 13:3 \fqa Shimeah \ft is a variant of \fqa Shammah\ft , \fqa Shimea\ft , and \fqa Shimei\ft ; see 1 Samuel 16:9, 2 Samuel 21:21, and 1 Chronicles 2:13.\f* \w Jonadab|strong="H03122"\w* \w was a very|strong="H03966"\w* \w shrewd|strong="H02450"\w* \w man|strong="H00376"\w*, \v 4 \w and he asked|strong="H00559"\w* [Amnon], “\w Why|strong="H04069"\w* \w are you|strong="H00859"\w*, \w the son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w so|strong="H03602"\w* \w depressed|strong="H01800"\w* \w morning|strong="H01242"\w* \w after morning|strong="H01242"\w*? \w Won’t|strong="H03808"\w* \w you tell|strong="H05046"\w* me?”
\p \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w replied|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w I am|strong="H00589"\w* \w in love|strong="H00157"\w* \w with Tamar|strong="H08559"\w*, \w my brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Absalom’s|strong="H00053"\w* \w sister|strong="H00269"\w*.”
\p \v 5 \w Jonadab|strong="H03082"\w* \w told|strong="H00559"\w* him, “\w Lie down|strong="H07901"\w* \w on|strong="H05921"\w* \w your bed|strong="H04904"\w* \w and pretend you are ill|strong="H02470"\w*. \w When your father|strong="H00001"\w* \w comes|strong="H00935"\w* \w to see you|strong="H07200"\w*, \w say|strong="H00559"\w* \w to him|strong="H00413"\w*, ‘\w Please|strong="H04994"\w* \w let my sister|strong="H00269"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w come|strong="H00935"\w* \w and give me something|strong="H01262"\w* \w to eat|strong="H03899"\w*. \w Let her prepare|strong="H06213"\w* \w [it]|strong="H01279"\w* \w in my sight|strong="H05869"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w so|strong="H04616"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w I may watch her|strong="H07200"\w* \w and eat it|strong="H00398"\w* \w from her hand|strong="H03027"\w*.’”
\p \v 6 \w So Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w lay down|strong="H07901"\w* \w and feigned illness|strong="H02470"\w*. \w When the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w came|strong="H00935"\w* \w to see him|strong="H07200"\w*, \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w -|strong="H00413"\w* \w -|strong="H04428"\w*, “\w Please|strong="H04994"\w* \w let my sister|strong="H00269"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03823"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w come|strong="H00935"\w* \w and make a couple|strong="H08147"\w* \w of cakes|strong="H03834"\w* \w in my sight|strong="H05869"\w*, \w so that I may eat|strong="H01262"\w* \w from her hand|strong="H03027"\w*.”
\p \v 7 \w Then David|strong="H01732"\w* \w sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w word to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w at the palace|strong="H01004"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w*: “\w Please|strong="H04994"\w* \w go|strong="H01980"\w* \w to the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w your brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w and prepare|strong="H06213"\w* \w a meal|strong="H01279"\w* for him.”
\p \v 8 \w So Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w went|strong="H01980"\w* \w to the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of her brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w*, \w [who]|strong="H01931"\w* \w was lying down|strong="H07901"\w*. \w She took|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w some dough|strong="H01217"\w*, \w kneaded [it]|strong="H03888"\w*, \w made cakes|strong="H03823"\w* \w in his sight|strong="H05869"\w*, \w and baked|strong="H01310"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w them|strong="H03834"\w*. \v 9 \w Then she brought|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the pan|strong="H04958"\w* \w and set it down|strong="H03332"\w* \w before him|strong="H06440"\w*, \w but he refused|strong="H03985"\w* \w to eat|strong="H00398"\w*. “\w Send everyone|strong="H03605"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00376"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w away|strong="H03318"\w*!” \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w*. \w And everyone|strong="H03605"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00376"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w went out|strong="H03318"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Then Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w*, “\w Bring|strong="H00935"\w* \w the food|strong="H01279"\w* \w into the bedroom|strong="H02315"\w*, \w so that I may eat it|strong="H01262"\w* \w from your hand|strong="H03027"\w*.”
\p \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w took|strong="H03947"\w* \w the cakes|strong="H03834"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w she had made|strong="H06213"\w* \w and went|strong="H00935"\w* \w to her brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Amnon’s|strong="H00550"\w* \w bedroom|strong="H02315"\w*. \v 11 \w And when she had brought [them]|strong="H05066"\w* \w to him|strong="H00413"\w* \w to eat|strong="H00398"\w*, \w he took hold|strong="H02388"\w* of her \w and said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Come|strong="H00935"\w* \w lie|strong="H07901"\w* \w with me|strong="H05973"\w*, \w my sister|strong="H00269"\w*!”
\p \v 12 “\w No|strong="H00408"\w*, \w my brother|strong="H00251"\w*!” \w she cried|strong="H00559"\w*. “\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w violate me|strong="H06031"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w such|strong="H03651"\w* \w a thing should never|strong="H03808"\w* \w be done|strong="H06213"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H03478"\w*. \w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w do|strong="H06213"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w this|strong="H02063"\w* \w disgraceful thing|strong="H05039"\w*! \v 13 \w Where|strong="H00575"\w* \w could I|strong="H00589"\w* \w ever take|strong="H01980"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w my shame|strong="H02781"\w*? \w And you|strong="H00859"\w* \w would be|strong="H01961"\w* \w like one|strong="H00259"\w* \w of the fools|strong="H05036"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H03478"\w*! \w . . .|strong="H06258"\w* \w Please|strong="H04994"\w* \w speak|strong="H01696"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w he will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w withhold me|strong="H04513"\w* \w from you|strong="H04480"\w*.”
\p \v 14 \w But [Amnon] refused|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00014"\w* \w to listen to her|strong="H08085"\w* \w . . .|strong="H06963"\w*, \w and being stronger|strong="H02388"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04480"\w*, \w he violated her|strong="H06031"\w* \w and lay with|strong="H07901"\w* \w her|strong="H00854"\w*.
\p \v 15 \w Then Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w hated [Tamar]|strong="H08130"\w* \w with such intensity|strong="H01419"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03966"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w his hatred|strong="H08135"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08130"\w* \w was greater than|strong="H01419"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08135"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w the love|strong="H00160"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w he previously had|strong="H00157"\w*. “\w Get up|strong="H06965"\w*!” \w he said|strong="H00559"\w* to her\w . . .|strong="H00550"\w*. “\w Be gone|strong="H01980"\w*!”
\p \v 16 “\w No|strong="H00408"\w*,” \w . . .|strong="H00182"\w* \w she replied|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w sending me away|strong="H07971"\w* \w [is worse] than|strong="H00312"\w* \w this|strong="H02063"\w* \w great|strong="H01419"\w* \w wrong|strong="H07451"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w you have already done|strong="H06213"\w* \w to me|strong="H05973"\w*!”
\p \w But he refused|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00014"\w* \w to listen|strong="H08085"\w* to her. \v 17 \w Instead, he called|strong="H07121"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w to his attendant|strong="H05288"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08334"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Throw|strong="H07971"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04994"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w this [woman]|strong="H02063"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w out|strong="H02351"\w* \w and bolt|strong="H05274"\w* \w the door|strong="H01817"\w* \w behind her|strong="H00310"\w*!”
\p \v 18 \w So Amnon’s attendant|strong="H08334"\w* \w threw|strong="H03318"\w* \w her|strong="H00853"\w* \w out|strong="H02351"\w* \w and bolted|strong="H05274"\w* \w the door|strong="H01817"\w* \w behind her|strong="H00310"\w*. \w Now Tamar was wearing|strong="H05921"\w* \w a robe|strong="H03801"\w* \w of many colors|strong="H06446"\w*,\f + \fr 13:18 \ft Or \fqa a robe with long sleeves\ft ; see also Genesis 37:3.\f* \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w this is what|strong="H03651"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w virgin|strong="H01330"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04598"\w* \w daughters|strong="H01323"\w* \w wore|strong="H03847"\w*. \v 19 \w And Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w put|strong="H03947"\w* \w ashes|strong="H00665"\w* \w on|strong="H05921"\w* \w her head|strong="H07218"\w* \w and tore|strong="H07167"\w* \w -|strong="H06446"\w* \w her|strong="H00834"\w* \w robe|strong="H03801"\w* \w -|strong="H05921"\w*. \w And putting|strong="H07760"\w* \w her hand|strong="H03027"\w* \w on|strong="H05921"\w* \w her head|strong="H07218"\w*, \w she went away|strong="H01980"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01980"\w* \w crying aloud|strong="H02199"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w Her brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Absalom|strong="H00053"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to her|strong="H00413"\w*, “\w Has your brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Amnon|strong="H00550"\w* \w been|strong="H01961"\w* \w with you|strong="H05973"\w*? \w Be quiet|strong="H02790"\w* \w for now|strong="H06258"\w*, \w my sister|strong="H00269"\w*. \w He|strong="H01931"\w* \w is your brother|strong="H00251"\w*. \w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w take|strong="H07896"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w this|strong="H02088"\w* \w thing|strong="H01697"\w* \w to heart|strong="H03820"\w*.”
\p \w So Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w lived|strong="H03427"\w* \w as a desolate|strong="H08076"\w* \w woman in the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of her brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Absalom|strong="H00053"\w*.
