\p \v 11 \w Two hundred|strong="H03967"\w* \w men|strong="H00376"\w* \w from Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w accompanied|strong="H01980"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00854"\w* \w Absalom|strong="H00053"\w*. \w They had been invited as guests|strong="H07121"\w* \w and they went along|strong="H01980"\w* \w innocently|strong="H08537"\w*, \w for they knew|strong="H03045"\w* \w nothing|strong="H03808"\w* \w about|strong="H03605"\w* \w the matter|strong="H01697"\w*. \v 12 \w While [Absalom] was offering|strong="H02076"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the sacrifices|strong="H02077"\w*, \w [he]|strong="H00053"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w sent for|strong="H07971"\w* \w Ahithophel|strong="H00302"\w* \w the Gilonite|strong="H01526"\w*, \w David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w counselor|strong="H03289"\w*, \w [to come] from his hometown|strong="H05892"\w* \w of Giloh|strong="H01542"\w*.
