\s1 Hushai’s Warning Saves David
\r (Psalm 55:1–23)
\p \v 15 \w So Hushai|strong="H02365"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w told|strong="H00559"\w* \w Zadok|strong="H06659"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w and Abiathar|strong="H00054"\w*, \w the priests|strong="H03548"\w*, “\w This is what|strong="H02063"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02063"\w* \w Ahithophel|strong="H00302"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w has advised|strong="H03289"\w* \w Absalom|strong="H00053"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and the elders|strong="H02205"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w and this is what|strong="H02063"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02063"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w have advised|strong="H03289"\w*. \v 16 \w Now|strong="H06258"\w* \w send|strong="H07971"\w* \w quickly|strong="H04120"\w* \w and tell|strong="H05046"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w spend|strong="H03885"\w* \w the night|strong="H03915"\w* \w at the fords|strong="H06160"\w* \w of the wilderness|strong="H04057"\w*, \w but|strong="H01571"\w* \w be sure to cross over|strong="H05674"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05674"\w*. \w Otherwise|strong="H06435"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w with him|strong="H00854"\w* \w will be swallowed up|strong="H01104"\w*.’”
