\p \v 24 \w Then Mephibosheth|strong="H04648"\w*, \w Saul’s|strong="H07586"\w* \w grandson|strong="H01121"\w*, \w went down|strong="H03381"\w* \w to meet|strong="H07122"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*. \w He had not|strong="H03808"\w* \w cared|strong="H06213"\w* \w for his feet|strong="H07272"\w* \w [or]|strong="H03808"\w* \w trimmed|strong="H06213"\w* \w his mustache|strong="H08222"\w* \w [or]|strong="H00853"\w* \w washed|strong="H03526"\w* \w his clothes|strong="H00899"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03808"\w* \w from|strong="H04480"\w* \w the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w had left|strong="H01980"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w he returned|strong="H00935"\w* \w safely|strong="H07965"\w*. \v 25 \w And|strong="H01961"\w* \w -|strong="H03588"\w* \w he came|strong="H00935"\w* \w from Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w to meet|strong="H07122"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w [who]|strong="H04428"\w* \w asked|strong="H00559"\w* him, “\w Mephibosheth|strong="H04648"\w*, \w why|strong="H04100"\w* \w did you not|strong="H03808"\w* \w go|strong="H01980"\w* \w with me|strong="H05973"\w*?”
