\s1 David’s Mighty Men
\r (1 Chronicles 11:10–47)
\p \v 8 \w These|strong="H00428"\w* \w are the names|strong="H08034"\w* \w of David’s|strong="H01732"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H01368"\w*:
\b 
\li1 \w Josheb-basshebeth|strong="H03429"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03429"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w the Tahchemonite|strong="H08461"\w*\f + \fr 23:8 \fqa Tahchemonite \ft is probably a variant of \fqa Hachmonite\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 11:11.\f* \w was chief|strong="H07218"\w* \w of the Three|strong="H07991"\w*.\f + \fr 23:8 \ft Or \fqa chief among the captains\f* \w He|strong="H01931"\w* \w wielded|strong="H05722"\w* \w his spear|strong="H06112"\w* \w against|strong="H05921"\w*\f + \fr 23:8 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 1 Chronicles 11:11); Hebrew \fqa He was called Adino the Eznite because of\f* \w eight|strong="H08083"\w* \w hundred [men]|strong="H03967"\w*, \w whom he killed|strong="H02491"\w* \w at one|strong="H00259"\w* \w time|strong="H06471"\w*.
\li1 \v 9 \w Next in command was|strong="H00310"\w* \w Eleazar|strong="H00499"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Dodo|strong="H01734"\w*\f + \fr 23:9 \fqa Dodo \ft is a variant of \fqa Dodai\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 27:4.\f* \w vvv|strong="H01121"\w* \w the Ahohite|strong="H00266"\w*. \w As one of the three|strong="H07969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H01368"\w*, \w he [went] with|strong="H05973"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w to taunt|strong="H02778"\w* \w the Philistines|strong="H06430"\w* \w who had gathered|strong="H00622"\w* \w for battle|strong="H04421"\w* \w [at Pas-dammim]|strong="H08033"\w*. \w The men|strong="H00376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w retreated|strong="H05927"\w*, \v 10 \w but Eleazar|strong="H01931"\w* \w stood his ground|strong="H06965"\w* \w and struck|strong="H05221"\w* \w the Philistines|strong="H06430"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03588"\w* \w his hand|strong="H03027"\w* \w grew weary|strong="H03021"\w* \w and stuck|strong="H01692"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03027"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w his sword|strong="H02719"\w*. \w The LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w brought about|strong="H06213"\w* \w a great|strong="H01419"\w* \w victory|strong="H08668"\w* \w that|strong="H01931"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w*. \w Then the troops|strong="H05971"\w* \w returned|strong="H07725"\w* \w to him|strong="H00310"\w*, \w but only|strong="H00389"\w* \w to plunder the dead|strong="H06584"\w*.
\li1 \v 11 \w And after him|strong="H00310"\w* \w was Shammah|strong="H08037"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Agee|strong="H00089"\w* \w the Hararite|strong="H02043"\w*. \w When the Philistines|strong="H06430"\w* \w had banded together|strong="H00622"\w* \w near|strong="H03896"\w* \w -|strong="H08033"\w* \w -|strong="H01961"\w* \w a field|strong="H02513"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07704"\w* \w full of|strong="H04392"\w* \w lentils|strong="H05742"\w*, \w [Israel’s] troops|strong="H05971"\w* \w fled|strong="H05127"\w* \w from|strong="H06440"\w* \w [them]|strong="H06430"\w*. \v 12 \w But [Shammah] took his stand|strong="H03320"\w* \w in the middle|strong="H08432"\w* \w of the field|strong="H02513"\w*, \w defended it|strong="H05337"\w*, \w and struck down|strong="H05221"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the Philistines|strong="H06430"\w*. \w So the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w brought about|strong="H06213"\w* \w a great|strong="H01419"\w* \w victory|strong="H08668"\w*.
\p \v 13 \w At|strong="H00413"\w* \w harvest time|strong="H07105"\w*, \w three|strong="H07970"\w* \w of the thirty|strong="H07970"\w* \w chief men|strong="H07218"\w* \w went down|strong="H03381"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w at|strong="H00413"\w* \w the cave|strong="H04631"\w* \w of Adullam|strong="H05725"\w*, \w while a company|strong="H02416"\w* \w of Philistines|strong="H06430"\w* \w was encamped|strong="H02583"\w* \w in the Valley|strong="H06010"\w* \w of Rephaim|strong="H07497"\w*. \v 14 \w At that time|strong="H00227"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w was in the stronghold|strong="H04686"\w*, \w and the garrison|strong="H04673"\w* \w of the Philistines|strong="H06430"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00227"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01035"\w* \w was at Bethlehem|strong="H01035"\w*. \v 15 \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w longed [for water]|strong="H00183"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Oh, that someone|strong="H04310"\w* \w would get me a drink|strong="H08248"\w* \w of water|strong="H04325"\w* \w from the well|strong="H00877"\w* \w near the gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01035"\w* \w of Bethlehem|strong="H01035"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w*!”
\p \v 16 \w So the three|strong="H07969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H01368"\w* \w broke|strong="H01234"\w* \w through the Philistine|strong="H06430"\w* \w camp|strong="H04264"\w*, \w drew|strong="H07579"\w* \w water|strong="H04325"\w* \w from the well|strong="H00877"\w* \w near the gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05375"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01035"\w* \w of Bethlehem|strong="H01035"\w*, \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w and brought [it]|strong="H00935"\w* \w back to|strong="H00413"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w*. \w But he refused|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00014"\w* \w to drink it|strong="H08354"\w*; \w instead , he poured it out|strong="H05258"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \v 17 \w saying|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Far be it|strong="H02486"\w* from me, \w O LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w to do|strong="H06213"\w* \w this|strong="H02063"\w*! \w Is [this not] the blood|strong="H01818"\w* \w of the men|strong="H00582"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01980"\w* \w who risked their lives|strong="H05315"\w*?” \w So he refused|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00014"\w* \w to drink it|strong="H08354"\w*.
\p \w Such|strong="H00428"\w* \w were the exploits|strong="H06213"\w* \w of the three|strong="H07969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H01368"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w Now Abishai|strong="H00052"\w*, \w the brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w of Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w and son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Zeruiah|strong="H06870"\w*, \w -|strong="H01931"\w* \w was chief|strong="H07218"\w* \w of the Three|strong="H07992"\w*,\f + \fr 23:18 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts (see also 1 Chronicles 11:20); two Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac \fqa the Thirty\f* \w and he|strong="H01931"\w* \w wielded|strong="H05782"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w his spear|strong="H02595"\w* \w against|strong="H05921"\w* \w three|strong="H07969"\w* \w hundred [men]|strong="H03967"\w*, \w killed [them]|strong="H02491"\w*, and won \w a name|strong="H08034"\w* \w along with [the] Three|strong="H07969"\w*. \v 19 \w Was he not|strong="H03588"\w* \w more honored|strong="H03513"\w* \w than|strong="H04480"\w* \w the Three|strong="H07969"\w*?\f + \fr 23:19 \ft Hebrew; Syriac \fqa the Thirty\f* \w And he became|strong="H01961"\w* their \w commander|strong="H08269"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H05704"\w* \w even though he was not|strong="H03808"\w* \w included|strong="H00935"\w* \w among the Three|strong="H07969"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w And Benaiah|strong="H01141"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Jehoiada|strong="H03077"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01121"\w* \w [was] a man|strong="H00376"\w* \w of valor|strong="H02416"\w*\f + \fr 23:20 \ft Or \fqa Benaiah son of Jehoiada was the son of Ishhai\f* \w from Kabzeel|strong="H06909"\w*, \w a man of many|strong="H07227"\w* \w exploits|strong="H06467"\w*. \w [He]|strong="H01931"\w* \w struck down|strong="H05221"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w two|strong="H08147"\w* \w champions|strong="H00739"\w*\f + \fr 23:20 \ft Or \fqa two sons of Ariel\f* \w of Moab|strong="H04124"\w*, \w and on a snowy|strong="H07950"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w* \w he|strong="H01931"\w* \w went down|strong="H03381"\w* \w into|strong="H08432"\w* \w a pit|strong="H00953"\w* \w and killed|strong="H05221"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w a lion|strong="H00738"\w*. \v 21 \w He|strong="H01931"\w* \w also struck down|strong="H05221"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w an Egyptian|strong="H04713"\w*, \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w a huge|strong="H04758"\w* \w man|strong="H00376"\w*. \w Although the Egyptian|strong="H04713"\w* \w had a spear|strong="H02595"\w* \w in his hand|strong="H03027"\w*, \w Benaiah went against|strong="H03381"\w* \w him|strong="H00413"\w* \w with a club|strong="H07626"\w*, \w snatched|strong="H01497"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the spear|strong="H02595"\w* \w from [his]|strong="H04713"\w* \w hand|strong="H03027"\w*, \w and killed [the Egyptian]|strong="H02026"\w* \w with his own spear|strong="H02595"\w*. \v 22 \w These|strong="H00428"\w* \w were the exploits|strong="H06213"\w* \w of Benaiah|strong="H01141"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Jehoiada|strong="H03077"\w*, who won \w a name|strong="H08034"\w* \w along with the three|strong="H07969"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H01368"\w*. \v 23 \w He was most honored|strong="H03513"\w* \w among|strong="H04480"\w* \w the Thirty|strong="H07970"\w*,\w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w but he did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w become|strong="H00935"\w* \w one of the Three|strong="H07969"\w*. \w And David|strong="H01732"\w* \w appointed him|strong="H07760"\w* \w over|strong="H00413"\w* \w his guard|strong="H04928"\w*.
\p \v 24 \w Now [these were members of] the Thirty|strong="H07970"\w*:\f + \fr 23:24 \ft Literally \fqa In the Thirty (were):\f*
