\s1 David’s Military Census
\r (Exodus 30:11–16; 1 Chronicles 21:1–6)
\p \v 1 \w Again|strong="H03254"\w* \w the anger|strong="H00639"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w burned|strong="H02734"\w* \w against Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w and He stirred up|strong="H05496"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* against them, \w saying|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Go|strong="H01980"\w* \w [and] take a census|strong="H04487"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and Judah|strong="H03063"\w*.”
\p \v 2 \w So the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w the commander|strong="H08269"\w* \w of his army|strong="H02428"\w*, \w who [was]|strong="H00834"\w* \w with him|strong="H00854"\w*,\f + \fr 24:2 \ft LXX \fqa to Joab and the army commanders with him\f* “\w Go|strong="H07751"\w* \w now|strong="H04994"\w* \w throughout|strong="H03605"\w* \w the tribes|strong="H07626"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w from Dan|strong="H01835"\w* \w to|strong="H05704"\w* \w vvv|strong="H00884"\w* \w Beersheba|strong="H00884"\w* \w and register|strong="H06485"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the troops|strong="H05971"\w*, \w so that I may know|strong="H03045"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w their number|strong="H04557"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05971"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w But Joab|strong="H03097"\w* \w replied|strong="H00559"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, “\w May the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w your God|strong="H00430"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w multiply|strong="H03254"\w* \w the troops|strong="H05971"\w* \w a hundred|strong="H03967"\w* \w times|strong="H06471"\w* over . . ., \w and may the eyes|strong="H05869"\w* \w of my lord|strong="H00113"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w see [it]|strong="H07200"\w*. \w But why|strong="H04100"\w* \w does my lord|strong="H00113"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w want|strong="H02654"\w* \w to do such|strong="H02088"\w* \w a thing|strong="H01697"\w*?”
